if you follow eSports then you've  probably noticed that competitions and  tournaments have been getting more and  more media attention from sports  websites some tournaments have even been  broadcasted on live television but it  looks like ESPN is doubling down on this  variety of sports today ESPN announced  and launched an internal division  dedicated to eSports the division is  appropriately called ESPN eSports and is  being pegged as a destination for  comprehensive coverage surrounding the  world of competitive gaming ESPN's  competitive gaming content will be live  on a special hub on espn's website ESPN  coms editor-in-chief chad millman said  you can expect ESPN's effort in the  gaming world to be of the same level of  quality content and journalism that  users of espn.com have come to expect  this will include in-depth looks at the  competitive gaming world and on-site  reporting from the major tournaments one  of ESPN's highest-profile business  riders Darren Rothwell is working on  esports content alongside a founding  staff member that includes former  GameSpot editor rod slasher Breslau  whether or not this means eSports will  get more airtime on ESPN's channels  remains to be seen for more gaming news  stay tuned to gamespot
 

